target: skills/review/review-loop/runlog.py
verify: cd skills/review/review-loop && ./runlog.test.sh
expect: FAIL  three n/a runs raise no alarm
why:    a gate with nothing to act on was not dropped, so `n/a` must not count against it in review-stats' alarm (the tier half lives in `looper record finish` now, pinned by looper's own goldens). This exact defect shipped — runlog's own comment records that a `status == "done"` test made every n/a a dropped gate and the Step 0 alarm fired permanently on gates nobody could fix, which teaches a reader to scroll past the alarms that are right
--- old
GATE_OK = ("done", "n/a")
--- new
GATE_OK = ("done",)
